          "text": "On admission the NIHSS was 9. CT head on Day 1 showed no haemorrhage, and the patient received thrombolysis with alteplase within the treatment window. Post-thrombolysis CT on Day 2 confirmed no bleed, and the NIHSS had improved to 4. Swallow was initially unsafe; SALT review was undertaken and nasogastric feeding commenced, with swallow recovering by Day 3. Anticoagulation with apixaban was started for AF per stroke protocol timing on Day 4, and aspirin was stopped. The early supported discharge (ESD) team accepted the patient.",
